This extension adds Hades II modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]Epic[/*]
[*]Xbox[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]

[size=3][b][color=#ea9999]This game does not support symlinks. You must have the mod staging folder and the game on the same drive to use this extension.[/color][/b][/size]

[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Mod Importer mods with a "modimporter.exe" file install to the "Content" folder.[/*]
[*]Mod Utility mods with a "modutil.lua" file install to the "Content\Mods\ModUtil" folder.[/*]
[*]Mod Loader (Hell2Modding) mods with a "d3d12.dll" file install to the "Ship" folder.[/*]
[*]Plugin mods are recognised by a "manifest.json" file and a "main.lua" file.[/*]
[*]Archives with a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*][b]Mod Loader (Hell2Modding)[/b] — Ship. Detected by d3d12.dll. Downloaded and installed automatically when the game is managed.[/*]
[*][b]Managed dependencies[/b] (ENVY (LuaENVY), ENVY (SGG Modding), Chalk, ReLoad, SJSON, DemonDaemon, ModUtil) — each installs to Ship&#92;ReturnOfModding&#92;plugins&#92; under its own mod type, and is downloaded automatically alongside the loader.[/*]
[*][b]Mod Importer[/b] (legacy, pre-1.0 ecosystem) — Content. Detected by modimporter.exe. Registered as a Dashboard tool so it can be launched after installing mods.[/*]
[/list]

[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for Hades II mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

Manager:

Recognised when the archive contains a "modimporter.exe" file.

  Installs to: "Content"

========================================================================

Modutility:

Recognised when the archive contains a "modutil.lua" file.

  Installs to: "Content\Mods\ModUtil"

========================================================================

Loader:

Recognised when the archive contains a "d3d12.dll" file.

  Installs to: "Ship"

========================================================================

Plugin:

Recognised when the archive contains a "manifest.json" file and a "main.lua" file.

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Archives containing a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to the built-in FOMOD installer instead.
    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine.
[/spoiler]

